- **F-5 (retrieval):** clause-NUMBER questions are semantically opaque to Titan v2 — "4.1" cannot rank the right chunk. Needs hybrid retrieval: parse explicit clause refs from questions → term filter on metadata.clauseRef (+ metadata.standard per guru), kNN otherwise.
- **F-6 (content depth):** corpus chunks are one-line paraphrases; any useful guru answer necessarily exceeds them → worst-segment-min grounding < 0.85 even with perfect retrieval. The guardrail chain is CORRECTLY refusing (honest-miss is designed behavior). Grounded expansive answers need per-clause guidance depth (content authoring — CertifyAero-gap territory), and/or a quote-first guru answer style. Threshold-lowering REJECTED (guts the anti-hallucination guarantee).
- Also logged: L1 source-injection retry consistently scores WORSE than pass 1 (0.15→0.01, 0.54→0.02) — retry mechanism worth revisiting in spec-35 carries.

